Q: How to properly close FIFO (named pipe) used in an infinite loop, when program terminates? A: <p>Just call the <code>unlink()</code> function in the client and server. But do not check the success of the operation, as the file may not exist, and then disconnection will fail, and the global variable errno will be set to <code>ENOENT</code></p>
<pre><code>int main(void) {
    unlink(&quot;&lt;filename&gt;&quot;);
